  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASSISTANCE D&apos;URGENCE EN ABRIS ET ARTICLES MENAGERS ESSENTIELS AUX PERSONNES AFFECT&#xC9;ES PAR LES ALEAS CLIMATIQUES AU BURUNDI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide emergency shelter and essential household items assistance to improve the living conditions and dignity of communities affected by the floods and landslides in Burundi. Key activities include distributing non-foot item kits and cash transfers covering shelter repair and rental assistance. The project provides life-saving assistance to 16,320 people, of whom 3,742 are women and 4,921 are girls. Additionally, 1,632 people with disabilities benefit from this project.</narrative>
  </description>
